($f$080b7013-14b2-4fd8-be8b-f567db3cdb39$f$, 12123849, $f$if the end comes (don't let us hear it)$f$, ARRAY[$f$Kandakicksass$f$]::text[], ARRAY[$f$Dishonored (Video Games)$f$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], $f$"He comes in like a ghost in the fall of 1854."***When the Outsider is freed from the void, he goes to Dunwall. Corvo finds him.$f$, 5026, 1, 1, true, 3, false, $f$2019-07-24T03:57:37.181+00:00$f$, $f$2019-07-24T03:57:37.468+00:00$f$, $f$2017-09-18T00:00:00.000+00:00$f$, false, false, true, NULL, NULL, ARRAY[]::text[]),
($f$080b7013-14b2-4fd8-be8b-f567db3cdb39$f$, 12133095, $f$I Am Unbreakable$f$, ARRAY[$f$SereneShadows$f$]::text[], ARRAY[$f$ジョジョの奇妙な冒険 | JoJo no Kimyou na Bouken | JoJo's Bizarre Adventure$f$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], NULL, NULL, 16, 16, true, -1, false, $f$2018-07-13T11:42:50.675+00:00$f$, $f$2018-07-13T11:42:50.741+00:00$f$, $f$2017-09-19T00:00:00.000+00:00$f$, false, false, true, NULL, NULL, ARRAY[]::text[]),
($f$080b7013-14b2-4fd8-be8b-f567db3cdb39$f$, 12138903, $f$Warmth$f$, ARRAY[$f$tveckling$f$]::text[], ARRAY[$f$Dishonored (Video Games)$f$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], $f$Voices speaking in quiet tones were all that could be heard from the room next door, and only if he concentrated could the Outsider hear which one belonged to Billie and which was Emily’s. At first he had perhaps expected shouts or yelling, but the small smile Emily threw Billie before they disappeared had removed that suspicion. Instead there was nothing but peacefulness; nothing to stop his mind from going in circles.Corvo was staring at him, silently, just like he had done ever since they had laid eyes on each other. Emily had been the one to talk, to ask questions and demand answers, while her father was as quiet as a statue. If it had been any other the Outsider supposed he would have felt uncomfortable or annoyed by the constant focus on him—but Corvo was different. Had always been, since he first caught the Outsider’s attention. The only source of irritation the Outsider felt was by his inability to look into Corvo’s mind and see what feelings were hiding there.$f$, 1536, 1, 1, true, 3, false, $f$2019-07-23T11:27:14.693+00:00$f$, $f$2019-07-23T11:27:15.011+00:00$f$, $f$2017-09-19T00:00:00.000+00:00$f$, false, false, true, NULL, NULL, ARRAY[]::text[]),
